<h4>The Landauer Erasure Machine</h4>
<p class="pnote">A single unknown, equiprobable bit, stored as a ball in a double-welled landscape: left = 0, right = 1. To <em>reset</em> it to 0 no matter where it started, you lower the wall, bias the landscape toward 0, and trap it left again — squeezing two possible pasts into one. In the ideal quasistatic limit, the work put into this irreversible reset is dissipated as heat; releasing the bias does not give the missing distinction back.</p>

